{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>These are the generations of the heavens and the earth when they were created</b> — It tells of the generations of the heavens and the earth through rain and vegetation, as they were created and made according to their arrangement, for the heavens give their dew and their rain and the earth gives its produce, and these are the sustenance of all life. And He hinted in <b>when they were created</b> (בהבראם) what they said concerning the letter ה\"א — that He created them (בה\"א בראם). And because of this, until now only the word Elohim was mentioned, and it is explicit in the verse (Isaiah 66:2), <b>and all these My hand has made</b>, and likewise Job said, <b>Who does not know among all these that the hand of YHWH has done this?</b> (Job 12:9). If so, <b>in the day that YHWH Elohim made</b> alludes to the word <b>Bereshith</b> (בראשית), as we have said."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:23:39.080422400Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}